{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "גדלים", :translit "gedilim", :gloss "twisted cords"} {:he "ב' הכא", :translit "bet kan", :gloss "two here"} {:he "ואידך גדלים", :translit "ve'idach gedilim", :gloss "and the other gedilim"} {:he "מעשה שרשרת", :translit "ma'aseh sharsheret", :gloss "work of chains"} {:he "גדיל", :translit "gadil", :gloss "twisted cord"} {:he "שנים", :translit "shnayim", :gloss "two"} {:he "דתרי גדלים כתיב", :translit "d'tarai gedilim katuv", :gloss "for two gedilim are written"} {:he "ופתלהו מתוכו", :translit "ufatlohu mitocho", :gloss "and twist it from within itself"} {:he "כדכתיב", :translit "kadkatuv", :gloss "as written"} {:he "מעשה שרשרות", :translit "ma'aseh sharsherot", :gloss "work of chains"} {:he "כדרך שעושים שרשרות", :translit "kederech she'osim sharsherot", :gloss "in the manner that chains are made"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["גדלים" "גדלים"]}], :frame {:text "The word גדלים appears twice in the Torah: once in Numbers 15:38 (regarding tzitzit) and once here in Deuteronomy 22:12. The term מעשה שרשרות, 'work of chains,' is a technical description in the Talmud for how the twisted cords of tzitzit must be formed — by twisting threads from within themselves rather than attaching a pre-made cord, analogous to chainwork where each link is formed from the material itself. The phrase ופתלהו מתוכו is used in Menachot 39a to describe this method.", :sources ["Numbers 15:38" "Deuteronomy 22:12" "Menachot 39a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אשר תכסה", :translit "asher techasseh", :gloss "which you cover yourself"} {:he "בכסות סומא", :translit "b'chisut suma", :gloss "in a blind person's garment"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אשר תכסה", :b "בכסות סומא"}], :frame {:text "A blind person's obligation in tzitzit is debated in the Talmud. The phrase בכסות סומא, 'a blind person's garment,' is equal in gematria to אשר תכסה, which serves as a scriptural hint supporting the position that a blind person is obligated in the mitzvah of tzitzit.", :sources ["Menachot 43b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אשר תכסה בה כי יקח", :translit "asher techasseh bah ki yikach", :gloss "which you cover yourself with, when he takes"} {:he "רמז להא דאיתא בנדרים", :translit "remez le'ha d'ita b'Nedarim", :gloss "a hint to that which is stated in Nedarim"} {:he "ר' אלעזר מגלה טפח ומכסה טפח בעת ביאה", :translit "Rabbi Elazar megaleh tefach umechasseh tefach b'et bi'ah", :gloss "Rabbi Elazar exposes a handbreadth and covers a handbreadth at the time of relations"} {:he "אשר תכסה כי יקח", :translit "asher techasseh ki yikach", :gloss "which you cover yourself, when he takes"} {:he "רמז לת\"ח שמאפיל בטליתו", :translit "remez l'TaCh she'me'apel b'talito", :gloss "a hint to a Torah scholar who darkens himself in his tallit"} {:he "כי יקח אשר תכסה", :translit "ki yikach asher techasseh", :gloss "when he takes, which you cover yourself"} {:he "מלמד שמכסים לו על כל עונותיו", :translit "m'lamed sh'mechassim lo al kol avonotav", :gloss "teaches that he is covered for all his sins"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Three remazim derived from varying the word order and juxtaposition of the phrase אשר תכסה כי יקח."}], :frame {:text "Rabbi Elazar's statement in Nedarim 20b addresses modest conduct during marital relations. The phrase about a Torah scholar wrapping himself in his tallit recalls descriptions of pious scholars who would cover themselves humbly, as noted in Shabbat 10a regarding scholars who appear cloaked in their garments. The third reading, reversing the word order to כי יקח אשר תכסה, homiletically teaches that one who takes this garment upon himself receives atonement for all sins, reflecting the theme in Menachot 44a that tzitzit brings protection from transgression.", :sources ["Nedarim 20b" "Shabbat 10a" "Menachot 44a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["גדלים" "גדלים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "גדלים", :refs ["Genesis 12:17" "Exodus 6:6" "Exodus 7:4" "Deuteronomy 4:34" "Deuteronomy 4:38" "Deuteronomy 6:22" "Deuteronomy 9:1" "Deuteronomy 11:23"], :n 23, :lens :exact} {:phrase "גדלים", :refs ["Genesis 12:17" "Exodus 6:6" "Exodus 7:4" "Deuteronomy 4:34" "Deuteronomy 4:38" "Deuteronomy 6:22" "Deuteronomy 9:1" "Deuteronomy 11:23"], :n 23, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "אשר תכסה", :a-value 986, :b "בכסות סומא", :b-value 595, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Three remazim derived from varying the word order and juxtaposition of the phrase אשר תכסה כי יקח.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:35.769110186Z", :model "glm-5.2"}